---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const globalData = await getEntry("global", "site");
if (!globalData) throw new Error("Global site data not found");
const { site } = globalData.data;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the HealthShores website and our medical tourism facilitation services."
  updated="9 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("<strong>Terms</strong>") apply to your use of www.healthshores.com (the
    "<strong>Website</strong>") and the medical tourism facilitation services provided by HealthShores, Bengaluru,
    India ("<strong>HealthShores</strong>", "<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>us</strong>"). By using the Website or our
    services, you agree to these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What we do</h2>
  <p>
    HealthShores is a <strong>facilitator</strong>. We help international patients find suitable hospitals and
    doctors in India and coordinate travel, accommodation and local support.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    We are not a hospital, clinic or healthcare provider, and we do not practise medicine. All diagnosis,
    treatment and medical decisions are made by independent, licensed hospitals and doctors, who are solely
    responsible for the medical care they provide.
  </div>

  <h2>2. Fees and payments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not charge patients for our facilitation services.</li>
    <li>
      All payments for treatment, including any deposit to book a procedure, are made directly to the hospital or
      provider, under their own terms, cancellation and refund policies.
    </li>
    <li>
      Travel, accommodation, visa and other third-party costs are paid to the relevant providers and are your
      responsibility unless agreed otherwise in writing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Cost estimates</h2>
  <p>
    Cost estimates are prepared by hospitals based on the information available at the time. They are not
    binding quotes. Final costs may change after in-person assessment, if your treatment plan changes, if your stay
    is extended, or if complications arise.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give complete and accurate information about your health, medical history and medications.</li>
    <li>
      Make sure your passport, visa and travel documents are valid. Visa decisions are made solely by the
      Government of India.
    </li>
    <li>Follow the instructions of your treating doctors, including pre-travel and post-treatment advice.</li>
    <li>Have appropriate travel and medical insurance where possible.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. No guarantee of outcomes</h2>
  <p>
    All medical treatment carries risk. We do not guarantee the result of any treatment, the availability of any
    doctor or hospital, or that any visa will be granted. Any figures on this Website about savings, success rates
    or outcomes are general information and not a promise about your case.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party providers</h2>
  <p>
    Hospitals, doctors, airlines, hotels, transport providers and other third parties are independent of
    HealthShores. Their services are governed by their own terms, and they are responsible for their own acts and
    omissions.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Website content</h2>
  <p>
    Content on the Website, including blog articles, is for general information only and is not medical advice.
    Please read our <a href="/disclaimer/">Medical Disclaimer</a>. We try to keep content accurate but do not
    guarantee that it is complete or up to date.
  </p>
  <p>
    The HealthShores name, logo and Website content belong to HealthShores and may not be copied or reused without
    our permission.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, HealthShores is not liable for any medical outcome, injury, loss or
    expense arising from treatment or services provided by hospitals, doctors or other third parties, or from your
    use of the Website. Nothing in these Terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle your personal and health information.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when they last changed.
    Continuing to use the Website or our services means you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of India. The courts of Bengaluru, Karnataka have exclusive jurisdiction
    over any dispute arising from them.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>HealthShores</strong><br />
    {site.address}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phone.replace(/\s/g, "")}`}>{site.phone}</a>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
